Hello Morton Grove residents, and welcome to your local news roundup from the Morton Grove Daily! Here is what is happening around our wonderful town this week.

Three local stories are making headlines:
1. The annual village park cleanup is scheduled for next Saturday morning, and local volunteers are encouraged to bring their own gardening gloves and trowels to help prep the community flower beds.
2. The public library has announced a brand new series of weekend crossword puzzle tournaments and board game afternoons for adults of all skill levels.
3. Construction on the Oak Street water main replacement project is slated to begin next Tuesday, so drivers should expect minor delays and plan alternate neighborhood routes accordingly.

Stay informed and stay connected with your neighbors!

